---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { gh, u } from '../lib/url';

// Two real runs, recorded 2026-09-27/28. Chapter times are seconds into each video; update them if a video is re-cut.
const runs = [
  {
    id: 'terminal',
    title: 'gate-api, in the terminal',
    lede: 'A small NodeJS service, from one XR to a canary on the prod cluster, with every command and every line of output shown as it really came back.',
    video: 'media/zero-to-running-terminal',
    chapters: [[0, 'Ask'], [19, 'Compose'], [59, 'Environments'], [89, 'Build'], [139, 'Dev'], [149, 'Staging'], [169, 'A real bug'], [209, 'Signed release'], [239, 'More bugs'], [279, 'Canary'], [325, 'The canary in Tower']] as [number, string][],
  },
  {
    id: 'tower',
    title: 'checkin-api, in Tower',
    lede: 'A small Python service, the same path again through Tower: the create form, a staging environment, a crash loop of my own making, the App Configuration tab, and the release.',
    video: 'media/zero-to-running-tower',
    chapters: [[0, 'Create'], [70, 'Onboarded'], [114, 'Staging environment'], [183, 'A crash loop'], [218, 'Configure staging'], [274, 'Release'], [301, 'Live on staging']] as [number, string][],
  },
];

const bugs = [
  {
    title: 'Four release gates ignored the new release file',
    text: "Since the release-file split, a release lands in <code>release.yaml</code>, but <code>sast</code>, <code>image-scan</code>, <code>sbom</code> and <code>provenance</code> still only looked at <code>values.yaml</code>. Every new app's first release would have failed.",
    href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/known-gaps.md'),
  },
  {
    title: 'Image promotion waited forever',
    text: "<code>image-promotion</code> waits for every gate, including the values check, and the values check never ran on a PR that only changed <code>release.yaml</code>.",
    href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/known-gaps.md'),
  },
  {
    title: 'The release relay address was wrong for a second machine',
    text: "Every release wrote the dev node's own address for the prod cluster to call back on, which it can't reach. I'd been fixing it by hand. It's now a per-cluster setting in the cluster registry.",
    href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/known-gaps.md'),
  },
  {
    title: "A new app's release hung before it started",
    text: "The release hooks run as a ServiceAccount that only exists when <code>releaseTracking</code> is set, and the ApplicationSet that creates it never read <code>release.yaml</code>. Every sync waited on a hook that couldn't start.",
    href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/known-gaps.md'),
  },
];
---
<Base title="Zero to running" description="Two real runs on Hangar, recorded: a new service from nothing to a canary in production, once in the terminal and once in Tower." section="platform">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Hangar, running · Two real runs</p>
      <h1>From nothing to <em>production</em>, for real</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        It's easy to draw a platform. These are two recordings of mine actually doing the work: a brand new service,
        from the first request to a canary on the prod cluster. Nothing is mocked. Waits are cut, cluster names are
        shown as dev and prod, and where something broke, it's left in.
      </p>
    </section>

    {runs.map((r) => (
      <section class="run" id={r.id}>
        <h2>{r.title}</h2>
        <p class="lede">{r.lede}</p>
        <figure class="video">
          <video controls playsinline muted preload="none" poster={u(`${r.video}-poster.jpg`)} width="1440" height="900">
            <source src={u(`${r.video}.webm`)} type="video/webm" />
            <source src={u(`${r.video}.mp4`)} type="video/mp4" />
            Your browser can't play this video. <a href={u(`${r.video}.mp4`)}>Download it instead</a>.
          </video>
        </figure>
        {r.chapters.length > 0 && (
          <nav class="chapters" aria-label={`${r.title} chapters`}>
            {r.chapters.map(([t, label]) => (
              <button type="button" data-t={t}><span class="t">{`${Math.floor(t / 60)}:${String(t % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`}</span>{label}</button>
            ))}
          </nav>
        )}
      </section>
    ))}

    <p class="principle">A demo that never breaks is a demo of the slides. The useful part is what the platform does when something is wrong.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What broke along the way</h2>
      <p>
        Running the whole path end to end, twice, found four real platform bugs that the individual tests hadn't. All
        four are fixed and written up in Glidepath's known gaps, and both videos end on the fixed path.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      {bugs.map((b) => (
        <a class="card" href={b.href}><span class="eyebrow"><span class="chip built">Fixed</span></span><h3>{b.title}</h3><p set:html={b.text} /></a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Two smaller things are still open. The <code>/retest</code> hint in the gate comments doesn't re-run a gate,
        and Tower showed my crash-looping pods as "Progressing" instead of saying why. Both are on the list.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want the design behind what you just watched? <a href={u('stack/')}>The stack</a> explains each tool, and
        <a href={u('cicd/')}>CI/CD</a> covers the delivery path in depth.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.run').forEach((run) => {
    const video = run.querySelector('video');
    run.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.chapters button').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (!video) return;
        video.currentTime = Number(b.dataset.t);
        video.play();
      }),
    );
  });
</script>

<style>
  .run { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .run h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .video { margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  .video video { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); background: var(--cockpit); box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18); }
  .chapters { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  .chapters button { font: inherit; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--ink); background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .chapters button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .chapters .t { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); margin-right: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .card .chip { font-size: 0.6rem; }
</style>
